title: Fix resource exhaustion when replaying finalized-block transactions
doc:
- audience:
  - Node Dev
  - Runtime Dev
  description: "# Description\n\nRe-applying the transactions of a finalized block\
    \ can yield different results than the original execution: transactions that originally\
    \ succeeded are rejected with `ExhaustsResources`. This affects runtime APIs that\
    \ replay a block (`pallet-revive`'s `trace_block` / `trace_tx`), where the rejected\
    \ tail transactions then produce no trace (a missing or zero-value phantom entry,\
    \ depending on the tracer).\n\n**The cause.** Each extrinsic is charged its declared\
    \ (worst-case) `proof_size`; `StorageWeightReclaim` then refunds the difference\
    \ between that and the actual proof size, which it reads from a proof-size recorder.\
    \ The original execution (at authoring) has a recorder registered, so the over-charge\
    \ is reclaimed and the block fits. The replay registers no recorder, so the proof-size\
    \ lookup returns nothing and reclaim is skipped. The declared `proof_size` accumulates\
    \ past the block limit and `CheckWeight` rejects the tail extrinsics. Reproduced\
    \ in an Asset Hub Westend integration test.\n\n**The fix.** Replay the block through\
    \ the runtime API with a proof-size recorder registered, so replay reproduces\
    \ the original execution and the whole block is processed.\n\n# Integration\n\n\
    - New **unsafe-gated** RPC `state_callRecorded` on `StateApi`, the recorded-replay\
    \ sibling of `state_traceBlock`.\n- New `TracingExecuteBlock::call_recorded` trait\
    \ method with a default impl that errors (non-breaking); implemented for parachains\
    \ in `cumulus-client-service`.\n- New `Error::CallRecordedUnsupported` and wire\
    \ code `CALL_RECORDED_UNSUPPORTED_ERROR_CODE` in `sc-rpc-api`.\n\n# Review Notes\n\
    \n**Approach.** `state_callRecorded` loads the block by hash, replays it from\
    \ parent state through a named runtime API with a proof-size recorder registered,\
    \ and returns the API's SCALE-encoded result (no tracing subscriber). The API's\
    \ first argument must be the replayed block; the node sources it and SCALE-prepends\
    \ it to `extra_args`.\n\n**Why a new RPC, not the existing call path.** `pallet-revive-eth-rpc`\
    \ talks to the node remotely, so its typed `runtime_api.trace_block()` already\
    \ crosses the wire as a `state_call`; the recorder can only be injected node-side.\
    \ `state_call` registers no recorder and offers no per-call hook to opt one in,\
    \ and registering a recorder on every `state_call` would change behaviour for\
    \ all callers. So we add one scoped, unsafe-gated method. When the node has the\
    \ authoring-time proof-size recording in its aux DB it is replayed for fidelity;\
    \ otherwise a fresh recorder is used.\n\n**Alternative approaches welcome.** This\
    \ is one way to give trace replay a recorder; suggestions for a different mechanism\
    \ or a smaller API surface are very welcome.\n\n**Client fallback.** When a node\
    \ cannot service `state_callRecorded` (method absent, or no recorder \u2014 e.g.\
    \ a solochain), eth-rpc falls back to the plain typed `trace_block`/`trace_tx`.\
    \ The fallback is not silent: version skew warns (the recorder-less replay can\
    \ still drop the tail on PoV chains), the expected recorder-less case logs at\
    \ debug.\n\n**Tests.** Integration tests in `asset-hub-westend` reproduce the\
    \ bug and confirm the fix. A block of two storage-heavy revive calls is replayed,\
    \ and the tail is traced only with a recorder registered:\n- `trace_block_drops_tail_trace_without_proof_recorder`\
    \ traces both calls with a recorder and fewer without;\n- `trace_tx_drops_tail_trace_without_proof_recorder`\
    \ traces the tail tx with a recorder and not without.\nA new `repeated_storage_read`\
    \ fixture creates the `proof_size` over-charge that triggers the drop.\nUnit tests\
    \ in `pallet-revive-eth-rpc` cover the fallback (which errors downgrade to a recorder-less\
    \ replay vs. propagate)."
crates:
- name: sc-tracing
  bump: minor
- name: cumulus-client-service
  bump: minor
- name: sc-rpc-api
  bump: major
- name: sc-rpc
  bump: major
- name: pallet-revive-eth-rpc
  bump: patch
- name: pallet-revive
  bump: patch
- name: asset-hub-westend-runtime
  bump: patch
- name: pallet-revive-fixtures
  bump: patch
